Date: Sat, 17 Jul 1993 21:59:30 -0400 (EDT)
From: Harry Shapiro <habs@panix.com>
Subject: Meta: Costs with the New list

A few days ago I mentioned our pending site move might cost us money.
I have got a few questions about that in private mail. I thought other
list members might also have similar questions.

Our use of a commercial site will cost more than use of GNU, but it is
quite worth it. (One gets what one pays for.)
_______________________________


Do I need more donations of money? No.

1) Several list members have offered to put up some money, which
combined with my own, is enough to get us started. It may be possible
that I will need a few more donations but this is unlikely.


Will it cost list members to use the list? No.

1) Given the current bandwidth we will be able to support up to a 50%
increase in average bandwidth before we would have to consider putting
in place a user fee or posting limit.

2) I am strongly committed to offering the basic features of our new
software to all list members as it has always been, at no cost.  Even
if I have to kick in more money.

3) Since CPU and bandwidth costs will go down in the next few years,
even if our usage goes up radically it is unlikely our real costs will
increase.


What about special features? Will they cost? Maybe

1) If we add CPU or bandwidth intensive features to the list they
might cost users on a strict usage fee basis (e.g., cover costs, ExI
overhead, etc. but no profit).

2) If you wish to design a high cost (CPU or Bandwidth) software agent
you will be liable for it's operating costs.

3) ExI members may be offered special software features as a premium
in return for their membership. This may include extra use of some of
the database features.


If I donate money to ExI specifically for the list what will I get?

1) You will get a bigger say in what features will added to the list
software.

2) You will certainly be consulted about new software features and
given advanced notice of our plans.

3) My personal thanks and mention in official ExI Publications will
also be extended.

4) Other "thanks" will be extended.

